From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: msm: dsi: use MSM8226 PHY regulator controls

MSM8226 factory DT supplies internal PHY regulator controls
[07 08 07 00 20 07 01]. The vendor PHY initialization explicitly maps
these seven bytes to CTRL0..CTRL5 and CAL_PWR_CFG. The common upstream
DCDC sequence instead programs CTRL1=09, CTRL2=03 and CTRL5=00.

Use the verified MSM8226 controls under the existing PHY_8226 quirk.
Preserve register order, CTRL0 initial disable, the calibration enable
and the separate LDO path. No external PMIC voltage is changed.
Native PLL lock and correct link clock rates alone have not established
physical DSI transmission on SM-T531; validate the analogue PHY separately.

Source: LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226 commit
3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256,
arch/arm/boot/dts/msm8226/dsi_panel_tc358764_wxga_video-r01.dtsi and
drivers/video/msm/mdss/msm_mdss_io_8974.c, mdss_dsi_phy_init().

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm.c
index d00e415b9..e7f021a98 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm.c
@@ -751,13 +751,14 @@ static void dsi_28nm_dphy_set_timing(struct msm_dsi_phy *phy,
 static void dsi_28nm_phy_regulator_enable_dcdc(struct msm_dsi_phy *phy)
 {
 	void __iomem *base = phy->reg_base;
+	bool msm8226 = phy->cfg->quirks & DSI_PHY_28NM_QUIRK_PHY_8226;
 
 	writel(0x0, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_0);
 	writel(1, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CAL_PWR_CFG);
-	writel(0, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_5);
+	writel(msm8226 ? 0x7 : 0, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_5);
 	writel(0, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_3);
-	writel(0x3, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_2);
-	writel(0x9, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_1);
+	writel(msm8226 ? 0x7 : 0x3, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_2);
+	writel(msm8226 ? 0x8 : 0x9, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_1);
 	writel(0x7, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_0);
 	writel(0x20, base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_REGULATOR_CTRL_4);
 	writel(0x00, phy->base + REG_DSI_28nm_PHY_LDO_CNTRL);
